## 6. Section 4 — Exposure Analysis

- Top Holdings via look-through (`utils.exposure.get_concentration_exposure`): for each ETF with weight `w_i`, contribution = `w_i × pct_{i,h}/100` summed across ETFs that hold underlying `h`. Sum is ≤ portfolio weight (some ETFs lack underlying data).
- Sector / Country (`utils.exposure.calculate_exposure`): `bucket_weight = Σ_i w_i × exp_{bucket,i}`, implemented as `df_exposure.dot(weights_aligned)`. Auto-detects 0-100 columns (sum > 1.5) and divides by 100. Missing tickers route to "Others"/asset-class fallback.
- Benchmark comparison plots use the same helper for the benchmark weight Series.

